# Planning and review MVP software design

Status: independently reviewed; implementation authorized. Product contract: PLAN.md and UI-REVIEW.md in this directory; written corrections override screenshots.

## Delivery checkpoints

The user's latest instruction authorizes independent-agent design and implementation checkpoints without waiting for the user overnight. R02 becomes an independently verified foundation gate. R03 remains the user's final acceptance in the running app; no agent will manufacture that approval. Design review must precede application edits. Implementation review must inspect actual source, tests and running UI before delivery.

## Ownership and persistence

1. Add one Planning contributor in app/planning.mjs. It owns planning tasks, inputs/discussions, typed relations, priorities, review requirements/outcomes and append-only revisions. Existing Harness task objects are execution sessions, not copies of planning tasks. Link session evidence with a session identifier and turn range; do not mirror titles/status from sessions into planning records or schedule sessions on a placement change.
2. Replace the planning input authority in Workflow with this owner. Preserve the existing eight inputs through a one-time owner-operated import, verify readback and archive the original document as immutable evidence before removing its inputs member. No permanent old-format loader or shadow write path. Existing contribution/session capture entry points call the owning input operation; their transport remains usable but is not another implementation of mutation rules. Existing conversation configuration, preview and feed settings remain Workflow-owned. Retire the mutable t.checkpoint/thread/outcome owner and its /api/checkpoint mutation route; preserve any existing checkpoint records as immutable execution evidence with original IDs, attribution and snapshot references. Continuing execution freeze/commit checks delegate to Planning; there is no second review lifecycle implementation. Remove exclusive old sample timeline and checkpoint UI/tests, replacing their substantive gate coverage with tests of the canonical owner.
3. Extract the existing decentralized manifest/entry/reference primitives from SystemsEngineering into a neutral exported RelationEngine serialization module and use them from both consumers. Preserve graph:// identities, graph.json manifests, entryDirectory, typed entry documents and URL-relative references. No runtime HTTP origin in identity. New app persistence writes complete immutable generations (manifest + entries + evidence), then atomically publishes one current-generation pointer. Serialize mutations through one promise queue; validate before publish; retain historical generations as revisions, not editable parallel stores. Startup never silently discards corrupt data. Failed publish preserves the previous pointer; orphan staging can be cleaned after validation. Resolve shared references by canonical URI, report unresolved references explicitly.
4. Every mutation has expected graph revision and requestId; validate the whole batch and reject stale writes atomically. Persist actor, command, request digest and result receipt with the generation. Same requestId/body is idempotent across restart; changed payload with same ID fails. Protected outcome, target and actor fields cannot be assigned through generic updates. Deleting referenced records requires explicit same-transaction removal of permissible relations; review/history references prevent deletion.
5. Typed node fields supply a reflected Node view: title, one description, purpose and placement where applicable. Immutable creator is a relation. Containment and prerequisite edges are independently acyclic, context-bound, navigable; continuation/responds-to/review-target relations have specialized validation. Authored relation types are declared in one owner schema used by tools and UI.

## Relational operations and tools

Compose a minimal RelationalEngine in the active app process with the existing Harness discovery contributor, Planning contributor and existing MCP transport. Declare direct local package dependencies on the engine, Harness and MCP packages; compile them explicitly. Do not revive the old full host or import package sources across undeclared boundaries.

Expose owner operations: read graph/schema/revisions/evidence, transactional node/relation/priority mutations, review lifecycle actions, discussion actions, granular run/stop checks, import/export. HTTP UI transport invokes the same engine operation definitions as MCP. Operation request JSON is validated by the owner; AgentUsage schema is generated from that same contract. Model transport credentials bind an agent actor and human UI credentials bind a human actor using AsyncLocalStorage around invocation. Operation callers cannot provide or promote actor identity.

Use the existing Broccoli Local endpoint configuration for an additional loopback MCP listener in the same process (no second owner), with a separately configured token and strict origin policy. Tests use ephemeral ports/tokens. Do not expose secrets in logs or the browser. Verify initialize/tools-list/tool-call and restart readback through the installed plugin's configured endpoint. If this Codex conversation cannot refresh tools, record that exact host limitation and exercise the real MCP endpoint rather than claim API-only calls are a model-tool demonstration.

## Review and evidence rules

Review is a task with a draft author-owned policy: exact target tasks, required/optional human reviewers and discovered runnable requirements. Submit captures immutable target node revisions and, for code review, the existing Buildspace snapshot (commit identifiers plus captured uncommitted contents). Branch names alone are never submitted identities. Record runnable definition identity and target fingerprint with each execution; requirement policy and temporal run events stay distinct.

Submitted, pending and blocked reviews freeze their scope; existing Checkpoints.assertEditable also consults the Planning owner for overlapping checkout locks. Planning edits consult submitted target revisions/containment. Corrections require all required reviewer outcomes before a changes-requested round releases its own freeze. Overlapping reviews keep their locks. Mandatory runnable success, human approvals and closure of every root discussion are required to pass. Optional failures remain visible. A human alone may accept stale *passed* evidence with a reason bound to this target; missing/failed/cancelled evidence cannot be waived as passed.

Each correction work task and subsequent review task is a distinct node. Continuation creation and later review creation are independently idempotent. A specialized successor operation atomically retargets enumerated pending gate edges to the new draft review with the same obligation, carries unresolved root comments by reference, preserves the failed result and logs actor/reason. Generic unlink cannot erase gate obligations. No synthetic future snapshot. Abandon is terminal nonpass. Passed reviews are sealed.

Comments are attributed input nodes; each root contains typed feedback rows, context/anchor and an optional preview. Replies link to the root/parent input. Only root-author closure gates the discussion; replies do not independently require closure. Actor-permitted edits/removals retain revision history. Reopening invalidates previous acceptance. Empty posts are rejected; anchors retain the submitted snapshot and file/line context.

Reuse Contributions/Buildspace repository check detection and check execution. A single granular operation resolves leaf IDs, deduplicates scopes and runs all/mandatory/selected; agent need not choose shell commands. Cancellation is scoped to active run groups and retains partial evidence. Submitted checks run in a disposable materialization of the exact submitted repository tree(s), overlaid with captured changes; dependency resolution uses isolated copies of repository-local package outputs/dependencies, never source-write-sharing links. Collect report/output evidence before cleanup. Missing base objects or unsupported dependency materialization produces an explicit unsupported result, never a fallback to the reviewed checkout. This isolates ordinary trusted check side effects, not malicious commands with arbitrary absolute paths; the application does not promise an OS sandbox. A source-mutating-check acceptance test proves the submitted checkout and immutable evidence remain unchanged. Fingerprint before/after inside the materialization prevents a mutating check from becoming clean passing evidence. Coverage presents available measured results and effective thresholds; never synthesize absent coverage. Shared cross-repository pipeline infrastructure stays B01.

## UI composition

Replace the sample checkpoint timeline entry with the real planning surface, preserving existing Files/Checks/Preview capabilities as reusable content renderers. Planning navigation has board and nested graph; selected-node views are Node/Graph/Review according to owner schema and relations. Existing buildspace navigation remains the host. Remove replaced sample fallback and its exclusive tests/styles.

Add reusable RelationalUi primitives only where missing: independent-column board/header composition, range-graph renderer/layout, typed feedback rows. Reuse Tree, SchemaForm, ViewToolbar/IconChoices, DataTable header controls and Splitter. The owner supplies labels, field descriptors, colors, relation semantics and actions; shared components contain no Broccoli vocabulary.

Board has independent Inputs/Backlog/Queued/Running/Blocked columns, no shared rows or top view toolbar. Backlog shows parentless tasks, inputs exclude task-parented discussion nodes. Queued brackets are stable-ID groups indexed 0..n; creating one requires members, empty groups disappear atomically. No drag MVP. Selection opens the right pane; empty selection leaves it blank. Actions provide full CRUD, nesting, dependencies and placement through schema-driven controls.

Graph occupies roughly one third; selected-node pane two thirds. Range rendering has endpoint dots, consistent purpose color, result only on the ending dot, actor involvement and no duration/cost. Layout preserves parallel branches/reviews and nests by containment. Continuation edges route from failed review end downward into next work start, laterally stacking the work/review loop; no Work/Review columns, arrowheads or boxed labels. Render actual relations only, never invent the golden sample topology in production. Test golden topology in a fixture and preserve a model-faithful relation list in Node before alternative layout is available. Breadcrumb drills into tasks; no task-group entity.

Node uses reflected fields and one flat relation list including creator. Toolbar has view selector, one revision dropdown and no/inline/side-by-side diff controls. Historical revisions are read-only; switching history never overwrites a live editor's expected revision. Drafts and selection/scroll persist across unrelated events. Missing references/evidence are explicit.

Review toolbar owns Overview/Changes/Preview tabs with no bottom gap, one revision selector and contextual tools. Its full-width toolbar sits above the inner activity/sidebar splitter. Overview has headerless typed-row composer, per-row trash, bottom actions, full-width top-level comments/previews and indented replies. Sidebar is Author/readiness then Checks > Reviewers/Runnables > Mandatory/Optional. Runnables is a normal tree row with right-aligned all/mandatory/selected/stop controls. Tree selection is click/Ctrl/Shift highlight; no checkboxes, per-row play or separate action/required columns. Results nest uniformly beneath every check. Requirements on the right, actual run events in the activity stream.

Changes reuses repository tree/editor/diff content with all/modified segmented control and iteration selection above the tree. Compose only selected iteration deltas; reject conflicting composition explicitly. Inline comments reuse feedback rows without duplicate diff preview. Preview reuses existing preview controls; historical unsupported previews are explicit, never silently live. No URL component, metrics or aggregate bottom panel.

## Bootstrap and verification

Import the complete canonical plan, software design, review dispositions, source hashes and reference images through the owner import operation with dry-run/commit and idempotent mapping receipt. Preserve all goals/criteria in descriptions and full source as immutable evidence. Read back after restart before replacing bootstrap files with a receipt. Subsequent task progress and review records use operations, not direct store edits.

Implementation batches: persistence/schema and serialization; relational/MCP/actor boundary; import/foundation review; reusable primitives and board/Node; graph and Review; real check/file integration; full acceptance and independent review. Record evidence against the corresponding imported tasks. No full completion is claimed from compilation alone.

Tests: atomic invalid/stale/concurrent mutation and crash/readback; graph identity after changed port; cycle and reference deletion; priority reorder/no execution; UI/MCP same contract and actor denial; reviewed scope/overlap/required outcomes/comment closure; rejected-review successor and inherited comments; immutable snapshot and stale evidence; runnable granularity/cancel; import complete/hash/retry; Node CRUD/history; independent scroll, drafts and keyboard tree selection; parallel/loop graph fixture; Overview/Changes/Preview real data. Run root test:all at checkpoints, declared contributor tests for touched packages, and inspect desktop/narrow screenshots. Independent implementation reviewer receives current design, diff/baseline, tests and known issues; discuss/revise until no material findings remain. Leave the real imported R03 review open for the user in the running app.

## Independent review disposition

Reviewer software_design_review received only the plan/design and inspected source. Round 1 identified canonical R02 drift, old checkpoint ownership and unsafe in-place check execution. Round 2 accepted retirement into immutable evidence and disposable submitted-tree execution for trusted checks (no OS sandbox promise). Canonical R02/procedure/verification text is reconciled with the latest user authorization; R03 remains human acceptance. No unresolved product question or material design finding remains. Implementation must provide the specified evidence; this approval does not certify unimplemented behavior.
